<rml>
<head>
	<!-- The map name splash (uimapnameshower.py): the name art of the map the
	     player entered at the top center, with the floor of the Demon Tower
	     or the Devil's Catacomb beside it. While the map-name flag is on, the
	     game window makes the facade nui_map_name.MapNameShower (controller
	     assets/root/nui_map_name.py). The fade is a keyframe animation (a
	     second's wait, the fade in, five seconds at 0.9, the fade out), which
	     each ShowMapName starts again by switching the body between two
	     animation classes; a format="none" nui-countdown hides the window at
	     its end. Under reduced motion it shows at 0.9 until the timer hides
	     it. The art is locale art (assets/locale). It takes no input. -->
	<title>map-name</title>
	<link type="text/template" href="../../nui.rtpl"/>
	<link type="text/rcss" href="map-name.rcss"/>
</head>
<body template="nui" class="nui-overlay map-name nui-anim" data-model="map_name"
	data-class-map-name--run-a="run == 'a'" data-class-map-name--run-b="run == 'b'">
	<div class="map-name__row" data-class-map-name__row--tower="offset == 'tower'"
		data-class-map-name__row--catacomb="offset == 'catacomb'">
		<img id="map-name" class="map-name__image" data-if="image != ''" data-attr-src="image"/>
	</div>
	<div class="map-name__row map-name__row--floor" data-if="floor_image != ''">
		<img id="map-floor" class="map-name__floor" data-attr-src="floor_image"/>
	</div>
	<nui-countdown id="map-name-timer" format="none" data-attr-end="hide_at" data-event-countdownend="done()"/>
</body>
</rml>
